/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  postDict -- the DETAILED SIZE of the separator drum (DEV.md 4c C318).

  `drum { ... }` replaces the residence-time basis.  Method `towler`: Towler &
  Sinnott 1st ed. section 10.9 (Eq. 10.10 u_t = 0.07 sqrt((rhoL - rhov)/rhov),
  x 0.15 without a demister; Eq. 10.11 D = sqrt(4 Qv / (pi u)); the vertical
  clearances of Figure 10.51a).  What the source does NOT fix is declared:
    holdupTime 600 s   Towler: "typically 10 minutes"
    surgeTime  60 s    ASSUMED -- the margin between normal and high level
    lowLevel   0.3 m   Towler Example 10.5: room for the level controller
    dropDiameter 150 um  ASSUMED design droplet, for the Haider-Levenspiel check
    nozzleVelocity     inside Towler section 5's windows (liquid 1-3 m/s,
                       vapour 15-30 m/s); the feed (two-phase) at 15 m/s
    diameterStep 0.1524 m  Wankat: "next largest 6-in. increment"
  `demister no`: the source's x 0.15 applies; `orientation vertical` is
  declared (leave it out and the drum chooses -- and prints why).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

sizing
{
    units
    (
        { unitName drum;  type vessel;  material SS304;
          designRules { pressureDesign 3.0;
                        corrosionAllow 0.003;  jointEfficiency 1.0;
                        drum { method towler;  demister yes;  orientation auto;
                               vapourStream vapor;  liquidStream liquid;
                               holdupTime 600;  surgeTime 60;  lowLevel 0.3;
                               diameterStep 0.1524;  dropDiameter 150e-6;
                               nozzleVelocity { feed 15;  vapour 20;  liquid 1.5; } } } }
    );
}
